# GREENSCALE -- black, then fifteen levels of phosphor green.
# P1 phosphor: the green of an Apple II monitor, an IBM 5151, a VT100's
# cousins.  Like AMBER.PAL this is a ramp, so it comes with a COLOR
# line: bright green on black.  Try COLOR A 0 for a tube that has
# been on since 1983.
#
# Entry 1 is not a step of the ramp: it is the shell's highlight (DIR's
# header and directories, labels, the banner) -- white on the VIC-II --
# so it is the brightest green, or those print black on black.  Text is
# E, one step down, so the highlight still stands out.
#
# index rr gg bb, all hex.  A file only changes the entries it names.
#
COLOR E 0
0 00 00 00
1 33 FF 33
2 07 22 07
3 0A 33 0A
4 0E 44 0E
5 11 55 11
6 14 66 14
7 18 77 18
8 1B 88 1B
9 1F 99 1F
A 22 AA 22
B 25 BB 25
C 29 CC 29
D 2C DD 2C
E 30 EE 30
F 33 FF 33
